<title>ITALY: POLL-ITALY SEEN AUCTIONING 4.5-6.0 TRLN LIRE BTPS.</title>
<headline>POLL-ITALY SEEN AUCTIONING 4.5-6.0 TRLN LIRE BTPS.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian Treasury is expected to issue between 4.5 and 6.0 trillion lire worth of medium and long-term fixed rate bonds (Btp) at its next auction on August 18, analysts polled by Reuters said.</p>
<p>Analysts forecast on average offer of 1.75 trillion lire for both the three and five-year Btp, and an average 1.75 trillion lire worth of the 30-year Btp.</p>
<p>The Treasury will be auctioning a 13th tranche of the May 15 2000 Btp, with a coupon of 6.0 percent, an 11th tranche of the 6.25 percent May 15 2002 Btp, and a 13th tranche of the 7.25 percent November 1 2026 Btp.</p>
<p>The Treasury will details the amounts to be offered on Tuesday. There are no expiring Btps at this time.</p>
<p>Following are the analysts' forecasts (in trillion lire):</p>
<p>			3-Yr Btp     5-Yr Btp     30-year Btp   TOTAL</p>
<p>Band of America     1.5	    1.5	    1.5	    4.5</p>
<p>Caboto		  1.5	    1.5	    2.0	    5.0</p>
<p>BCI		     2.0	    2.0	    2.0	    6.0</p>
<p>Credito Italiano    2.0	    2.0	    1.0	    5.0</p>
<p>Deutsche Bank	 2.0	    2.0	    2.0	    6.0</p>
<p>J.P. Morgan	   1.5	    1.5	    1.5	    4.5</p>
<p>================================================================</p>
<p>CONSENSUS	     1.75	   1.75	   1.75	   5.25</p>
<p>================================================================</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom 00392 66128589</p>
